{
    include "registries/aaosa.hocon",
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Broker submission intake-completeness checking with synthetic policy data. Deterministic Python tools own readiness status; agents may only assist with narrative. No underwriting, pricing, acceptance, rejection, or email sending.",
        "tags": ["insurance", "broker-submissions", "synthetic-data", "human-review"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Check policy POL-1001 for missing information and material changes.",
            "Summarize a complete broker submission for underwriter review.",
        ]
    },

    "instructions_prefix": """
This application checks only broker-submission intake completeness. It does not perform
underwriting, pricing, risk selection, acceptance, or rejection. Never invent or alter a
readiness status: use ReadinessDecisionTool and report its exact deterministic result.
Use synthetic policy data only. Never send an email; the Email Agent drafts text for
human review only.
""",

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "broker_submission_readiness",
            "function": {
                "description": "Coordinates deterministic checks and creates supplemental narrative for a broker submission."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "query": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "A JSON-encoded submission and request for an intake-completeness review."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["query"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Delegate policy retrieval, required-field/document checks, policy comparison, and
completeness status to their named specialist agents. The completion status returned by
Readiness Decision Agent is authoritative and deterministic. Summaries and email text
are drafts only. Do not make an underwriting or risk-selection decision.
""",
            "tools": [
                "policy_context_agent",
                "submission_validation_agent",
                "consistency_agent",
                "readiness_decision_agent",
                "summary_agent",
                "email_agent",
                "explainability_agent"
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "policy_context_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Retrieves the requested policy from synthetic local JSON data."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Call PolicyLookupTool with the policy number from the request. Do not claim to contact a
live IBM i system.
""",
            "tools": ["PolicyLookupTool"]
        },
        {
            "name": "PolicyLookupTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Returns one synthetic policy record from the local policy JSON file."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "policy_number": {"type": "string", "description": "Synthetic policy number."}
                    },
                    "required": ["policy_number"]
                }
            },
            "class": "readiness_tools.PolicyLookupTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "submission_validation_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Checks required submission fields and documents using deterministic Python rules."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Call SubmissionValidationTool. Report its missing fields, missing documents, and input
errors without guessing or hiding a missing item.
""",
            "tools": ["SubmissionValidationTool"]
        },
        {
            "name": "SubmissionValidationTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Deterministically validates required fields and documents."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "policy_number": {"type": "string"},
                        "submission": {"type": "object", "description": "Structured submission object."}
                    },
                    "required": ["policy_number", "submission"]
                }
            },
            "class": "readiness_tools.SubmissionValidationTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "consistency_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Compares submission values with current policy values and flags material changes."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Call ConsistencyCheckTool and report its field comparisons as supplied. A material change
is a flag for a human underwriter, not an acceptance, rejection, or risk assessment.
""",
            "tools": ["ConsistencyCheckTool"]
        },
        {
            "name": "ConsistencyCheckTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Returns deterministic field-by-field policy comparisons."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "policy_number": {"type": "string"},
                        "submission": {"type": "object", "description": "Structured submission object."}
                    },
                    "required": ["policy_number", "submission"]
                }
            },
            "class": "readiness_tools.ConsistencyCheckTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "readiness_decision_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Gets the authoritative deterministic completeness status."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Call ReadinessDecisionTool using the exact validation output. Return its readiness_status
verbatim. This is only an intake completeness label, never an underwriting decision.
""",
            "tools": ["ReadinessDecisionTool"]
        },
        {
            "name": "ReadinessDecisionTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Deterministically decides whether required intake information is complete."
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "missing_fields": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}},
                        "missing_documents": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}},
                        "field_errors": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}
                    },
                    "required": ["missing_fields", "missing_documents", "field_errors"]
                }
            },
            "class": "readiness_tools.ReadinessDecisionTool"
        },
        {
            "name": "summary_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Writes a concise supplemental summary using only supplied report facts."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Write a short summary from the supplied report. Do not create, change, or infer the
readiness status. Do not recommend coverage, pricing, acceptance, rejection, or risk
selection. Make clear this is intake completeness for human review.
"""
        },
        {
            "name": "email_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Drafts broker follow-up text without sending email."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Draft concise broker correspondence from supplied missing fields and documents only. Never
send the message, invoke a mail service, or claim the message was sent. The human must
review and approve before copying.
"""
        },
        {
            "name": "explainability_agent",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Explains deterministic validation and materiality rules."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Explain only the supplied triggered rule identifiers and their rule descriptions. Do not
invent additional rules or a policy outcome.
"""
        }
    ]
}
